{"id":"mahabharata-12-296","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":296,"title":"षण्णवत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 296 · The twenty-fifth and the twenty-sixth","summary":{"en":"Vasishtha explains the unmanifest which holds the qualities, and how the twenty-fifth, though awake, may still be unwise as long as he is not awake to the twenty-sixth. He tells the king that, having crossed the unfathomable unmanifest, he is free from dust and darkness, and the king is enlightened.","kn":"ಗುಣಗಳನ್ನು ಧರಿಸುವ ಅವ್ಯಕ್ತವನ್ನು ವಿವರಿಸಿ ಇಪ್ಪತ್ತೈದನೆಯವನು ಎಚ್ಚರವಾಗಿದ್ದರೂ ಇಪ್ಪತ್ತಾರನೆಯವನ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಎಚ್ಚರವಿಲ್ಲದಿರುವವರೆಗೆ ಅಜ್ಞಾನಿಯಾಗಿರುತ್ತಾನೆಂದು ವಸಿಷ್ಠ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅಗಾಧ ಅವ್ಯಕ್ತವನ್ನು ದಾಟಿದ ರಾಜ ರಜಸ್ಸು-ತಮಸ್ಸು ಮುಕ್ತನೆಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"वसिष्ठ गुणों को धारण करने वाले अव्यक्त का स्पष्टीकरण देते हैं और कहते हैं कि पच्चीसवाँ जागा हुआ होकर भी तब तक अज्ञानी रह सकता है जब तक वह छब्बीसवें के प्रति न जागे। वे राजा से कहते हैं कि अगाध अव्यक्त को पार कर वह रज और तम से मुक्त है।","te":"గుణాలను ధరించే అవ్యక్తాన్ని వివరించి, ఇరవై ఐదవవాడు మేల్కొన్నా ఇరవై ఆరవవాని పట్ల మేల్కొనని వరకు అజ్ఞానిగా ఉండవచ్చని వసిష్ఠుడు చెబుతాడు. అగాధ అవ్యక్తాన్ని దాటిన రాజు రజస్సు, తమస్సుల నుండి ముక్తుడని చెబుతాడు.","ta":"குணங்களைத் தாங்கும் வெளிப்படாததை விளக்கி, இருபத்தைந்தாமவன் விழிப்புடன் இருந்தாலும் இருபத்தாறாமவனை அறியும் வரை அறிவிலியாக இருக்கலாம் என்று வசிஷ்டர் கூறுகிறார். ஆழமான வெளிப்படாததைக் கடந்த மன்னன் ரஜஸ் தமஸிலிருந்து விடுபட்டவன் என்கிறார்.","ml":"ഗുണങ്ങളെ ഉൾക്കൊള്ളുന്ന അവ്യക്തത വസിഷ്ഠൻ വിശദീകരിക്കുന്നു; ഇരുപത്തിയാറാമനെക്കുറിച്ച് ഉണരാത്തിടത്തോളം, ഉണർന്നിരിക്കുമ്പോഴും ഇരുപത്തിഅഞ്ചാമൻ അജ്ഞനായിരിക്കാമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. അളക്കാനാകാത്ത അവ്യക്തത കടന്നവൻ പൊടിയിൽനിന്നും ഇരുട്ടിൽനിന്നും മോചിതനാകുന്നുവെന്നും, അങ്ങനെ രാജാവ് പ്രബുദ്ധനായെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം രാജാവിനോട് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.296; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"वसिष्ठ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasishtha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अप्रबुद्धमथाव्यक्तमिमं गुणविधिं शृणु ।\nगुणान्धारयते ह्येषा सृजत्याक्षिपते तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now hear this rule of the qualities concerning the unawakened unmanifest: she holds the qualities, and she sends them forth and draws them back."}},{"n":2,"text":"अजस्रं त्विह क्रीडार्थं विकुर्वन्ती नराधिप ।\nआत्मानं बहुधा कृत्वा तान्येव च विचक्षते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ceaselessly, king, she transforms herself here for play, making herself manifold, and those very forms are what they perceive."}},{"n":3,"text":"एतदेवं विकुर्वाणां बुध्यमानो न बुध्यते ।\nअव्यक्तबोधनाच्चैव बुध्यमानं वदन्त्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The awakening one does not awaken to her as she thus transforms; yet because of awakening to the unmanifest, they call him the awakening one."}},{"n":4,"text":"न त्वेव बुध्यतेऽव्यक्तं सगुणं वाथ निर्गुणम् ।\nकदाचित्त्वेव खल्वेतदाहुरप्रतिबुद्धकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Still, he does not truly awaken to the unmanifest, whether with or without qualities; at times they indeed call this the unawakened."}},{"n":5,"text":"बुध्यते यदि वाव्यक्तमेतद्वै पञ्चविंशकम् ।\nबुध्यमानो भवत्येष सङ्गात्मक इति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the twenty-fifth does awaken to the unmanifest, then, as the tradition says, he becomes the awakening one, of the nature of attachment."}},{"n":6,"text":"अनेनाप्रतिबुद्धेति वदन्त्यव्यक्तमच्युतम् ।\nअव्यक्तबोधनाच्चैव बुध्यमानं वदन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"By this they call the unmanifest imperishable \"unawakened\"; and because of awakening to the unmanifest they call him the awakening one."}},{"n":7,"text":"पञ्चविंशं महात्मानं न चासावपि बुध्यते ।\nषड्विंशं विमलं बुद्धमप्रमेयं सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor does even he awaken to the great-souled twenty-fifth; the twenty-sixth is stainless, awakened, immeasurable and eternal."}},{"n":8,"text":"सततं पञ्चविंशं च चतुर्विंशं च बुध्यते ।\nदृश्यादृश्ये ह्यनुगतमुभावेव महाद्युती ॥","meaning":{"en":"The twenty-sixth ever knows both the twenty-fifth and the twenty-fourth, the two great radiances that follow the seen and the unseen."}},{"n":9,"text":"अव्यक्तं न तु तद्ब्रह्म बुध्यते तात केवलम् ।\nकेवलं पञ्चविंशं च चतुर्विंशं न पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"But, dear one, that Brahman does not know the unmanifest alone; it is alone, and does not see the twenty-fifth or the twenty-fourth."}},{"n":10,"text":"बुध्यमानो यदात्मानमन्योऽहमिति मन्यते ।\nतदा प्रकृतिमानेष भवत्यव्यक्तलोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the awakening one thinks of himself, \"I am other,\" then he possesses Nature, with the eyes of the unmanifest."}},{"n":11,"text":"बुध्यते च परां बुद्धिं विशुद्धाममलां यदा ।\nषड्विंशो राजशार्दूल तदा बुद्धत्वमाव्रजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And when the twenty-sixth, tiger among kings, awakens to the supreme, pure, spotless intelligence, he then attains awakenedness."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततस्त्यजति सोऽव्यक्तं सर्गप्रलयधर्मिणम् ।\nनिर्गुणः प्रकृतिं वेद गुणयुक्तामचेतनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he abandons the unmanifest, which is subject to creation and dissolution, and, qualityless, knows Nature as endowed with qualities and unconscious."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततः केवलधर्मासौ भवत्यव्यक्तदर्शनात् ।\nकेवलेन समागम्य विमुक्तोऽऽत्मानमाप्नुयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, through seeing the unmanifest, he becomes of the nature of aloneness; joined with the alone, being freed, he attains the Self."}},{"n":14,"text":"एतत्तत्तत्त्वमित्याहुर्निस्तत्त्वमजरामरम् ।\nतत्त्वसंश्रयणादेतत्तत्त्ववन्न च मानद ।\nपञ्चविंशतितत्त्वानि प्रवदन्ति मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They call this the principle; the principle-less is ageless and deathless. Because it relies on principles it is not truly possessed of principles, honorable one; the wise speak of twenty-five principles."}},{"n":15,"text":"न चैष तत्त्ववांस्तात निस्तत्त्वस्त्वेष बुद्धिमान् ।\nएष मुञ्चति तत्त्वं हि क्षिप्रं बुद्धस्य लक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is not possessed of principles, dear one; this wise one is principle-less. He quickly lets go of the principle; this is the mark of the awakened."}},{"n":16,"text":"षड्विंशोऽहमिति प्राज्ञो गृह्यमाणोऽजरामरः ।\nकेवलेन बलेनैव समतां यात्यसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am the twenty-sixth,\" the wise one, held to be ageless and deathless, comes undoubtedly to equality by the strength of aloneness alone."}},{"n":17,"text":"षड्विंशेन प्रबुद्धेन बुध्यमानोऽप्यबुद्धिमान् ।\nएतन्नानात्वमित्युक्तं सांख्यश्रुतिनिदर्शनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through the twenty-sixth, who is awakened, the one awakening yet unwise is told of; this is what is called manyness, from the illustration in the Sankhya tradition."}},{"n":18,"text":"चेतनेन समेतस्य पञ्चविंशतिकस्य च ।\nएकत्वं वै भवत्यस्य यदा बुद्ध्या न बुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the twenty-fifth, joined with the conscious, does not awaken through intellect, oneness arises for him."}},{"n":19,"text":"बुध्यमानोऽप्रबुद्धेन समतां याति मैथिल ।\nसङ्गधर्मा भवत्येष निःसङ्गात्मा नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"The awakening one, king of Mithila, comes to equality with the unawakened; he becomes of the nature of attachment, whereas the other is of detached nature."}},{"n":20,"text":"निःसङ्गात्मानमासाद्य षड्विंशकमजं विदुः ।\nविभुस्त्यजति चाव्यक्तं यदा त्वेतद्विबुध्यते ।\nचतुर्विंशमगाधं च षड्विंशस्य प्रबोधनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the detached Self they know the unborn twenty-sixth. The all-pervading one abandons the unmanifest when he understands this, and the unfathomable twenty-fourth, through awakening to the twenty-sixth."}},{"n":21,"text":"एष ह्यप्रतिबुद्धश्च बुध्यमानश्च तेऽनघ ।\nप्रोक्तो बुद्धश्च तत्त्वेन यथाश्रुतिनिदर्शनात् ।\nनानात्वैकत्वमेतावद्द्रष्टव्यं शास्त्रदृष्टिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This one, sinless king, has been described to you as unawakened, awakening and awakened, in truth, according to the tradition; so much of manyness and oneness is to be seen by those who see by the treatises."}},{"n":22,"text":"मशकोदुम्बरे यद्वदन्यत्वं तद्वदेतयोः ।\nमत्स्योऽम्भसि यथा तद्वदन्यत्वमुपलभ्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the gnat and the fig tree are different, so are these two; as the fish in the water, so their otherness is perceived."}},{"n":23,"text":"एवमेवावगन्तव्यं नानात्वैकत्वमेतयोः ।\nएतद्विमोक्ष इत्युक्तमव्यक्तज्ञानसंहितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In just this way the manyness and oneness of the two are to be understood; this is called liberation, joined with knowledge of the unmanifest."}},{"n":24,"text":"पञ्चविंशतिकस्यास्य योऽयं देहेषु वर्तते ।\nएष मोक्षयितव्येति प्राहुरव्यक्तगोचरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This one who dwells in the bodies, of the twenty-fifth, is to be freed,\" they say, from the range of the unmanifest."}},{"n":25,"text":"सोऽयमेवं विमुच्येत नान्यथेति विनिश्चयः ।\nपरेण परधर्मा च भवत्येष समेत्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is freed in just this way and not otherwise; this is settled. Joining with the supreme, he becomes of supreme nature."}},{"n":26,"text":"विशुद्धधर्मा शुद्धेन बुद्धेन च स बुद्धिमान् ।\nविमुक्तधर्मा मुक्तेन समेत्य पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joined with the pure, the awakened and the freed, O best of men, the wise one becomes pure in nature, awakened and freed in nature."}},{"n":27,"text":"नियोगधर्मिणा चैव नियोगात्मा भवत्यपि ।\nविमोक्षिणा विमोक्षश्च समेत्येह तथा भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By joining the one bound by duty he becomes bound to duty, and by joining the liberator he attains liberation here."}},{"n":28,"text":"शुचिकर्मा शुचिश्चैव भवत्यमितदीप्तिमान् ।\nविमलात्मा च भवति समेत्य विमलात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"He becomes pure in deeds and pure, of limitless splendor, and, joining the spotless Self, his own self becomes spotless."}},{"n":29,"text":"केवलात्मा तथा चैव केवलेन समेत्य वै ।\nस्वतन्त्रश्च स्वतन्त्रेण स्वतन्त्रत्वमवाप्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, joined with the alone, he becomes alone in self, and joining the independent, the independent attains independence."}},{"n":30,"text":"एतावदेतत्कथितं मया ते\nतथ्यं महाराज यथार्थतत्त्वम् ।\nअमत्सरत्वं प्रतिगृह्य चार्थं\nसनातनं ब्रह्म विशुद्धमाद्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This much I have told you, great king, truly, as the real principle: having accepted this meaning without envy, you have the eternal, pure and primal Brahman."}},{"n":31,"text":"न वेदनिष्ठस्य जनस्य राज-\nन्प्रदेयमेतत्परमं त्वया भवेत् ।\nविवित्समानाय विबोधकारकं\nप्रबोधहेतोः प्रणतस्य शासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, you should not give this supreme teaching to a man not devoted to the Veda; it is for one who seeks to know and bows, an instruction that gives awakening for the sake of awakening."}},{"n":32,"text":"न देयमेतच्च तथानृतात्मने\nशठाय क्लीबाय न जिह्मबुद्धये ।\nन पण्डितज्ञानपरोपतापिने\nदेयं त्वयेदं विनिबोध यादृशे ॥","meaning":{"en":"It should not be given to one false in spirit, nor to a rogue, a weakling or a crooked mind, nor to one who torments the learning of the wise. Understand to whom you should give it."}},{"n":33,"text":"श्रद्धान्वितायाथ गुणान्विताय\nपरापवादाद्विरताय नित्यम् ।\nविशुद्धयोगाय बुधाय चैव\nक्रियावतेऽथ क्षमिणे हिताय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give it to one full of faith and virtue, always refraining from slander, of pure Yoga, wise, active, patient and well-wishing."}},{"n":34,"text":"विविक्तशीलाय विधिप्रियाय\nविवादहीनाय बहुश्रुताय ।\nविजानते चैव न चाहितक्षमे\nदमे च शक्ताय शमे च देहिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give it to one of secluded conduct, fond of rule, free of quarrel, widely learned, discerning, not tolerant of harm to others, and capable of self-control and of calm among embodied beings."}},{"n":35,"text":"एतैर्गुणैर्हीनतमे न देय-\nमेतत्परं ब्रह्म विशुद्धमाहुः ।\nन श्रेयसा योक्ष्यति तादृशे कृतं\nधर्मप्रवक्तारमपात्रदानात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This supreme pure Brahman should not be given to one lacking these qualities; one who gives to an unworthy person, speaking dharma, will not be joined with good."}},{"n":36,"text":"पृथ्वीमिमां यद्यपि रत्नपूर्णां\nदद्यान्नदेयं त्विदमव्रताय ।\nजितेन्द्रियायैतदसंशयं ते\nभवेत्प्रदेयं परमं नरेन्द्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if one were to give this whole earth full of jewels, this is not to be given to one who keeps no vows; but to one of conquered senses, lord of men, this supreme teaching may undoubtedly be given."}},{"n":37,"text":"कराल मा ते भयमस्तु किंचि-\nदेतच्छ्रुतं ब्रह्म परं त्वयाद्य ।\nयथावदुक्तं परमं पवित्रं\nनिःशोकमत्यन्तमनादिमध्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karala, let you have no fear at all; you have today heard the supreme Brahman, stated truly, highest and purifying, free of sorrow, without beginning, middle or end."}},{"n":38,"text":"अगाधजन्मामरणं च राज-\nन्निरामयं वीतभयं शिवं च ।\nसमीक्ष्य मोहं त्यज चाद्य सर्वं\nज्ञानस्य तत्त्वार्थमिदं विदित्वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, it is of fathomless birth and death, free of ailment, fearless and auspicious. Having considered it, abandon all delusion today, knowing this to be the truth of knowledge."}},{"n":39,"text":"अवाप्तमेतद्धि पुरा सनातना-\nद्धिरण्यगर्भाद्गदतो नराधिप ।\nप्रसाद्य यत्नेन तमुग्रतेजसं\nसनातनं ब्रह्म यथाद्य वै त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, this was obtained long ago from the eternal Hiranyagarbha as he spoke, by pleasing that fierce-splendored one with effort, just as you have today sought the eternal Brahman."}},{"n":40,"text":"पृष्टस्त्वया चास्मि यथा नरेन्द्र\nतथा मयेदं त्वयि चोक्तमद्य ।\nतथावाप्तं ब्रह्मणो मे नरेन्द्र\nमहज्ज्ञानं मोक्षविदां पुराणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As you asked me, king of men, so I have told you this today, just as I received from Brahma the great and ancient knowledge of those who know liberation."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"एतदुक्तं परं ब्रह्म यस्मान्नावर्तते पुनः ।\nपञ्चविंशो महाराज परमर्षिनिदर्शनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This supreme Brahman, from which there is no return, has been told, great king; the twenty-fifth is taught by the illustration of the great seers."}},{"n":42,"text":"पुनरावृत्तिमाप्नोति परं ज्ञानमवाप्य च ।\nनावबुध्यति तत्त्वेन बुध्यमानोऽजरामरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who has reached supreme knowledge yet returns again; the awakening one, ageless and deathless, does not truly awaken."}},{"n":43,"text":"एतन्निःश्रेयसकरं ज्ञानानां ते परं मया ।\nकथितं तत्त्वतस्तात श्रुत्वा देवर्षितो नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"This, the highest of knowledges, which brings the supreme good, I have told you truly, dear one, having heard it from the divine sage."}},{"n":44,"text":"हिरण्यगर्भादृषिणा वसिष्ठेन महात्मना ।\nवसिष्ठादृषिशार्दूलान्नारदोऽवाप्तवानिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From Hiranyagarbha the great-souled sage Vasishtha received it; from Vasishtha, tiger among sages, Narada received it."}},{"n":45,"text":"नारदाद्विदितं मह्यमेतद्ब्रह्म सनातनम् ।\nमा शुचः कौरवेन्द्र त्वं श्रुत्वैतत्परमं पदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From Narada this eternal Brahman became known to me. Do not grieve, lord of the Kurus, having heard this supreme state."}},{"n":46,"text":"येन क्षराक्षरे वित्ते न भयं तस्य विद्यते ।\nविद्यते तु भयं तस्य यो नैतद्वेत्ति पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who knows the perishable and imperishable has no fear; but fear belongs to the one, king, who does not know this."}},{"n":47,"text":"अविज्ञानाच्च मूढात्मा पुनः पुनरुपद्रवन् ।\nप्रेत्य जातिसहस्राणि मरणान्तान्युपाश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through ignorance the deluded one, harassed again and again, after death undergoes thousands of births ending in death."}},{"n":48,"text":"देवलोकं तथा तिर्यङ्मानुष्यमपि चाश्नुते ।\nयदि शुध्यति कालेन तस्मादज्ञानसागरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He goes to the world of the gods, and also to animal and human birth, unless in time he is purified from that ocean of ignorance."}},{"n":49,"text":"अज्ञानसागरो घोरो ह्यव्यक्तोऽगाध उच्यते ।\nअहन्यहनि मज्जन्ति यत्र भूतानि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ocean of ignorance is terrible, called unmanifest and fathomless, in which beings sink day after day, Bharata."}},{"n":50,"text":"यस्मादगाधादव्यक्तादुत्तीर्णस्त्वं सनातनात् ।\nतस्मात्त्वं विरजाश्चैव वितमस्कश्च पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since you have crossed over from that fathomless, eternal unmanifest, therefore you are free of dust and free of darkness, king."}}]}]}